{
  "name": "Competitor Stealth Radar — New Trademark Filing Alerts",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Competitor Stealth Radar — new trademark filing alerts\n### How it works\nCompanies file trademarks months before they announce a product, feature, or sub-brand. Every Monday this workflow checks the companies on your watchlist against the official USPTO database (via the USPTO Trademark Search actor on Apify), spots filings that are new since the last run, has an AI explain in plain English what each filing probably signals, and posts one alert per filing to Slack. Every filing found is written to your Log sheet, and that log is the memory: a filing whose serial number is already logged is never alerted twice. Only filings from the last 14 days are fetched, so weekly runs stay cheap.\n### Setup\n1. Make a Google Sheet with two tabs: Watchlist (one column, ownerName — the exact USPTO owner name of each competitor) and Log (columns: serialNumber, wordmark, owner, filedDate, internationalClasses, goodsAndServices, aiSummary, dateLogged).\n2. Point both Sheets read nodes and the Log append node at your sheet and connect your Google account.\n3. Connect your Apify account in the search node, a Gemini key in the chat model (or swap in another model), and your Slack workspace and channel in the alert node.\n### Customization\nWiden lookback_days in the settings node for a longer window, raise max_results_per_competitor for very large filers, or change the Monday schedule.",
        "width": 920,
        "height": 320
      },
      "name": "Sticky st1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -320
      ],
      "id": "st1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚠️ Don't delete Log rows\nThe Log tab is this workflow's memory. Deleting rows makes those filings look new again, and they will re-alert on the next run.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 140,
        "color": 3
      },
      "name": "Sticky st2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        620
      ],
      "id": "st2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 · Watchlist & settings\nThe settings node holds the lookback window and the per-competitor cap. The Watchlist tab lists the exact USPTO owner names to track, and the Log tab is read once per run so already-seen filings can be filtered out.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 380,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Sticky st3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        200
      ],
      "id": "st3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 · Check each competitor\nCompetitors are checked one at a time. For each one, the actor searches USPTO by owner name, live marks only, filed inside the window. The filter then keeps only filings whose serial number is not already in the Log.",
        "width": 730,
        "height": 380,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Sticky st4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        900,
        200
      ],
      "id": "st4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 · Explain the filing\nEach genuinely new filing goes to the LLM, which reads the goods and services text and drafts a short, plain-English guess at what the competitor is building and why it matters. The alert text and the log row are assembled next.",
        "width": 730,
        "height": 380,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Sticky st5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1650,
        200
      ],
      "id": "st5"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 · Alert, then log\nOne Slack message per new filing — never a digest. The filing is appended to the Log only after its alert has been sent, so if a run fails mid-way the filing is re-alerted next week instead of being lost silently.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 380,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Sticky st6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2400,
        200
